commit 655c2211ed00bb422c30ec1306f2bc8ea0ec660c

C03: the system-microphone question is guided from the start and validated as an offer (UI1657)

UI1655 measured the client-scoped microphone clarification: the reader fired on all six requests, but the small model, guided only by the field name and a one-shot correction, asked to confirm a state or which microphone, dropped the system microphone, or exhausted both wordings; the validator also forbade the subjunctive «silencie» the right offer needs. A system message now explains the field from the start (BAXY does not operate the application's mute button; it can only mute the Windows system microphone, and the application would stop receiving it) and the validator requires an offer («¿querés que silencie…?», «would you like me to mute…?») while rejecting state confirmations, which-microphone questions and claims of a mute already done.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


